{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:45:35.722Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**What was done:**\n\n1. **`src/core/spec/approve-seal-restore.ts`** (new, in scope): the keep-and-restore helpers —\n   - `snapshotSealFiles` keeps the bytes of `.run/approved`, `.run/manifest.json`, `.run/plan.jsonl` (or absence) before the approval writes them;\n   - `restoreSealFiles` puts each file back, deleting one that was absent;\n   - `approvalCommitLanded` takes an object with only a `show` method, reads `show('HEAD', '<change folder>/.run/approved')`, and reports whether HEAD holds the new hash;\n   - `commitFailedError` builds `the approved commit failed in <worktree root>: <git error>. The approval seal is undone and the plan edits are kept; run osq approve <id> again.`\n\n2. **`src/core/spec/approve-steer.ts`**: `approveSteeredChange` snapshots the seal files before `appendObservedSessions`, wraps the commit in try/catch, checks `approvalCommitLanded` first — on a landed commit it keeps the seal and continues to `retireSteering`; otherwise it restores the seal files, retires no trigger, and throws the requirement's error. No `Vcs` injection seam was added; the function is 72 lines (under the 80-line budget) and carries `@scenario spec-lint-and-approve: Approved commit fails`.\n\n3. **`tests/approve-steer-commit-failed.test.ts`** (new): a plain `node:test` file proving \"Approved commit fails\" end-to-end via `createRecoveryProject`/`ScriptedAdapter`/`reviseTask` (stuck task reached as `recovery-stuck-steer` does), creating the file `git rev-parse --git-path index.lock` names in the worktree before `project.approve()` and removing it in a `finally`. Every THEN clause is asserted: exit 1 with the three phrases; the three seal files byte-identical to before; edited `tasks/1.md` unchanged; `.run/dead/1.md` in place; HEAD unchanged. The same file unit-tests `approvalCommitLanded` with plain objects (`new hash + newline` → keep; old hash / null → roll back).\n\nBoth the task verify and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`, exit 0) pass."}}
